{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Fyqfs1S9dsSxk7TuJCHvqq","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tid: srd083-truncate\n2\ttitle: \"cmd/truncate: Shrink or Extend File Size\"\n3\t\n4\tproblem: |\n5\t  macOS ships a BSD truncate that differs from GNU truncate in flag syntax and relative\n6\t  size adjustment support. The Go implementation must match the Homebrew GNU reference\n7\t  binary (gtruncate, installed by coreutils) byte-for-byte on all flag combinations,\n8\t  verified by differential testing via pkg/testutils.\n9\t\n10\tgoals:\n11\t  - G1: Set or adjust the size of files.\n12\t  - G2: Support absolute and relative size specifications with unit suffixes.\n13\t  - G3: Support reference file sizing.\n14\t  - G4: Verify functional parity against gtruncate via differential testing.\n15\t\n16\trequirements:\n17\t  R1:\n18\t    title: Size specification\n19\t    items:\n20\t      - R1.1:\n21\t          text: \"-s SIZE or --size=SIZE must set each FILE's size to SIZE bytes. SIZE may include unit suffixes (K, M, G, T, P, E, Z, Y for powers of 1024; KB, MB, GB for powers of 1000).\"\n22\t      - R1.2:\n23\t          text: \"SIZE may be prefixed with + or - for relative adjustment (grow or shrink), < to set at most SIZE, > to set at least SIZE, / to round down to multiple, % to round up to multiple.\"\n24\t      - R1.3:\n25\t          text: Must process multiple FILE arguments, applying the same size operation to each.\n26\t      - R1.4:\n27\t          text: \"-c or --no-create must not create files that do not exist. Without -c, missing files are created.\"\n28\t\n29\t  R2:\n30\t    title: Reference file\n31\t    items:\n32\t      - R2.1:\n33\t          text: \"-r RFILE or --reference=RFILE must use the size of RFILE as the base size instead of an explicit SIZE. Can be combined with -s for relative adjustment from the reference size.\"\n34\t      - R2.2:\n35\t          text: Must exit 1 if the reference file cannot be accessed.\n36\t\n37\t  R3:\n38\t    title: Exit codes and SIGPIPE\n39\t    items:\n40\t      - R3.1:\n41\t          text: Must exit 0 when all files are processed successfully.\n42\t      - R3.2:\n43\t          text: Must exit 1 when any file cannot be opened, created, or resized, or when SIZE is invalid.\n44\t      - R3.3:\n45\t          text: Must handle SIGPIPE gracefully (exit 0) using pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler.\n46\t\n47\tnon_goals:\n48\t  - cmd/truncate does not implement sparse file optimization.\n49\t\n50\tpackage_contract:\n51\t  imports:\n52\t    - github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sizeparse\n53\t    - github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\n54\t\n55\tacceptance_criteria:\n56\t  - id: AC1\n57\t    criterion: \"truncate -s 100 file creates or resizes file to 100 bytes, matching gtruncate.\"\n58\t    traces:\n59\t      - R1.1\n60\t      - R1.3\n61\t      - R1.4\n62\t  - id: AC2\n63\t    criterion: \"truncate -s +50 file grows file by 50 bytes, matching gtruncate.\"\n64\t    traces:\n65\t      - R1.2\n66\t  - id: AC3\n67\t    criterion: \"truncate -r ref file sets file to ref's size, matching gtruncate.\"\n68\t    traces:\n69\t      - R2.1\n70\t  - id: AC4\n71\t    criterion: \"Differential test against gtruncate passes for all required test cases.\"\n72\t    traces:\n73\t      - R1.1\n74\t      - R1.2\n75\t      - R1.3\n76\t      - R2.1\n77\t  - id: AC5\n78\t    criterion: \"cmd/truncate compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n79\t    traces:\n80\t      - R1.1\n81\t      - R1.2\n82\t      - R1.3\n83\t      - R1.4\n84\t      - R2.1\n85\t      - R2.2\n86\t      - R3.1\n87\t      - R3.2\n88\t      - R3.3\n89\t\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_011HUmmhJdN1udvm4vihaJ6o","session_id":"5d300cbb-1173-48e1-93b4-4f506bd94bc9","uuid":"f0f348c4-4b9c-4821-993f-3a4c1ef22370","timestamp":"2026-05-23T16:35:21.500Z"}
