ile support\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet — code has not been written.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Key design tension identified: Task says implement only R1.1-R1.4, but acceptance criteria AC5 requires `go test ./cmd/truncate/ -count=1` to pass, and the test file includes R2 (reference file) tests. Solution: implement the full utility including R2 and R3 to pass all tests.\n   - The `<`, `>`, `/`, `%` prefix modifiers are NOT handled by sizeparse — truncate must strip these prefixes before calling `ParseWithOptions` and then apply the operation semantics after getting the parsed size value.\n   - sizeparse handles `+`/`-` signs when `AllowSign: true` is set.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - First message: The complete task prompt with project context, SRD, execution constitution, coding standards, and task specification for implementing cmd/truncate core size operations.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Create `cmd/truncate/main.go` implementing the truncate utility\n   - Must handle: flag parsing (`-s`/`--size`, `-c`/`--no-create`, `-r`/`--reference`), size prefix modifiers (`+`, `-`, `<`, `>`, `/`, `%`), unit suffix parsing via sizeparse, multiple file processing, reference file sizing, proper exit codes, SIGPIPE handler\n   - Run `go build -o bin/truncate ./cmd/truncate/` to verify compilation\n   - Run `go vet ./cmd/truncate/` to verify no warnings\n   - Run `go test ./cmd/truncate/ -count=1` to verify all differential tests pass\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I had just finished gathering all required context by reading the SRD (srd083-truncate.yaml), the existing test file (truncate_test.go), and the sizeparse package (parse.go) via two parallel Explore agents. Both agents returned successfully with complete file contents. I was about to begin implementing `cmd/truncate/main.go` — the sole file to create for this task.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Create `cmd/truncate/main.go` implementing the full truncate utility. The implementation needs to:\n