{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019jgh3eejqeFTEgrNc1ck25","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! I now have all the information I need. Let me provide you with a comprehensive breakdown of how the DiffTest struct works:\n\n## DiffTest Struct Fields\n\nThe `DiffTest` struct (lines 46-55 in difftest.go) has the following fields:\n\n1. **Name** (string): Identifies the subtest, used with `t.Run()`\n2. **Args** ([]string): Command-line arguments passed to both binaries\n3. **Stdin** ([]byte): Input data for stdin\n   - `nil` = both binaries receive EOF immediately\n   - Empty non-nil slice `[]byte{}` = open stdin immediately closed\n4. **Env** ([]string): Environment variable overrides in KEY=VALUE format\n   - `nil` = inherit test process environment with `LC_ALL=C` applied as default\n   - Non-nil = merged into inherited environment (matching keys are overridden)\n5. **WorkDir** (string): Working directory for test execution\n6. **ExitCode** (int): Expected exit code (defaults to 0)\n7. **Normalize** ([]NormalizeFunc): Slice of normalizer functions applied in order to stdout/stderr before comparison\n8. **ExpectedFiles** (map[string][]byte): Expected file contents to validate after execution\n\n## How RunDiffTests Executes Tests\n\nThe `RunDiffTests` function (lines 83-90) orchestrates the testing:\n\n1. **Execution Flow**: For each test case, it calls `runSubtest` which:\n   - Determines the working directory (line 94-97):\n     - If `tc.WorkDir` is empty, creates a **temporary directory** via `t.TempDir()`\n     - Otherwise, uses the provided `WorkDir`\n   - Builds an environment map (line 98) with `LC_ALL=C` as a default override\n   - **Executes both binaries in the same WorkDir** with identical inputs (lines 99-100)\n   - Applies all normalizer functions to both results (lines 101-102)\n   - Compares outputs (line 103)\n   - Validates expected files (line 104)\n\n2. **Binary Execution** (lines 107-128 in `runBinary`):\n   - Uses `exec.CommandContext` with a 10-second timeout\n   - Sets `cmd.Dir = workDir` (line 116)\n   - Captures stdout and stderr separately\n   - If stdin is non-nil, pipes it to the binary\n   - Extracts exit code from `exec.ExitError` or returns 0 on success\n\n## File Argument Resolution\n\nThe file argument handling is in `checkExpectedFiles` (lines 211-227):\n\n- **ExpectedFiles keys are treated as relative paths**\n- **Resolution**: `fullPath := filepath.Join(workDir, relPath)` (line 217)\n- This means files are resolved relative to the working directory where the binaries executed\n- The test reads each expected file from disk and compares its contents byte-for-byte with the expected value\n\n## Key Execution Details\n\n- **Both binaries run in the same working directory** (either the provided `WorkDir` or a temp dir)\n- **Environment is identical** for both: merged from inherited environment + test-provided overrides + `LC_ALL=C`\n- **Comparison happens AFTER normalization**: normalizers can strip timestamps or other volatile content before comparison\n- **Files are validated AFTER execution**: the test checks that files exist and match expected contents in the working directory where the commands ran\n- **Timeout is hardcoded to 10 seconds** (`defaultTimeout` at line 24)"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5d300cbb-1173-48e1-93b4-4f506bd94bc9","uuid":"a0fe2738-c875-4af5-a00b-f2e848fe10b3","timestamp":"2026-05-23T16:37:32.910Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"I need to understand how the DiffTest struct works in pkg/testutils, specifically:\n1. What fields does DiffTest have (especially WorkDir, ExpectedFiles, Normalize, ExitCode)?\n2. How does RunDiffTests execute tests — does it run in WorkDir or a temp dir? Does it compare files?\n3. How does it handle the \"file\" argument — does it resolve relative to the working dir?\n\nRead pkg/testutils/diff.go and any related files. Give me the key details about how tests are executed.","agentId":"a725a0f99d07d5147","agentType":"Explore","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! I now have all the information I need. Let me provide you with a comprehensive breakdown of how the DiffTest struct works:\n\n## DiffTest Struct Fields\n\nThe `DiffTest` struct (lines 46-55 in difftest.go) has the following fields:\n\n1. **Name** (string): Identifies the subtest, used with `t.Run()`\n2. **Args** ([]string): Command-line arguments passed to both binaries\n3. **Stdin** ([]byte): Input data for stdin\n   - `nil` = both binaries receive EOF immediately\n   - Empty non-nil slice `[]byte{}` = open stdin immediately closed\n4. **Env** ([]string): Environment variable overrides in KEY=VALUE format\n   - `nil` = inherit test process environment with `LC_ALL=C` applied as default\n   - Non-nil = merged into inherited environment (matching keys are overridden)\n5. **WorkDir** (string): Working directory for test execution\n6. **ExitCode** (int): Expected exit code (defaults to 0)\n7. **Normalize** ([]NormalizeFunc): Slice of normalizer functions applied in order to stdout/stderr before comparison\n8. **ExpectedFiles** (map[string][]byte): Expected file contents to validate after execution\n\n## How RunDiffTests Executes Tests\n\nThe `RunDiffTests` function (lines 83-90) orchestrates the testing:\n\n1. **Execution Flow**: For each test case, it calls `runSubtest` which:\n   - Determines the working directory (line 94-97):\n     - If `tc.WorkDir` is empty, creates a **temporary directory** via `t.TempDir()`\n     - Otherwise, uses the provided `WorkDir`\n   - Builds an environment map (line 98) with `LC_ALL=C` as a default override\n   - **Executes both binaries in the same WorkDir** with identical inputs (lines 99-100)\n   - Applies all normalizer functions to both results (lines 101-102)\n   - Compares outputs (line 103)\n   - Validates expected files (line 104)\n\n2. **Binary Execution** (lines 107-128 in `runBinary`):\n   - Uses `exec.CommandContext` with a 10-second timeout\n   - Sets `cmd.Dir = workDir` (line 116)\n   - Captures stdout and stderr separately\n   - If stdin is non-nil, pipes it to the binary\n   - Extracts exit code from `exec.ExitError` or returns 0 on success\n\n## File Argument Resolution\n\nThe file argument handling is in `checkExpectedFiles` (lines 211-227):\n\n- **ExpectedFiles keys are treated as relative paths**\n- **Resolution**: `fullPath := filepath.Join(workDir, relPath)` (line 217)\n- This means files are resolved relative to the working directory where the binaries executed\n- The test reads each expected file from disk and compares its contents byte-for-byte with the expected value\n\n## Key Execution Details\n\n- **Both binaries run in the same working directory** (either the provided `WorkDir` or a temp dir)\n- **Environment is identical** for both: merged from inherited environment + test-provided overrides + `LC_ALL=C`\n- **Comparison happens AFTER normalization**: normalizers can strip timestamps or other volatile content before comparison\n- **Files are validated AFTER execution**: the test checks that files exist and match expected contents in the working directory where the commands ran\n- **Timeout is hardcoded to 10 seconds** (`defaultTimeout` at line 24)"}],"totalDurationMs":19888,"totalTokens":26627,"totalToolUseCount":11,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6310,"cache_read_input_tokens":19464,"output_tokens":846,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":6310},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":7,"output_tokens":846,"cache_read_input_tokens":19464,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6310,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":6310,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"toolStats":{"readCount":7,"searchCount":1,"bashCount":3,"editFileCount":0,"linesAdded":0,"linesRemov